ed Nirvana upon these very ridges.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"betla-national-park\",\n    name: \"Betla National Park\",\n    tagline: \"Ancient Sal forests, tigers & 16th-century Chero forts\",\n    category: \"Wildlife & Nature\",\n    district: \"Latehar\",\n    location: \"Palamu District border, 160 km from Ranchi\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.8824,\n      lng: 84.1887\n    },\n    elevation: \"350 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"November to April\",\n    timings: \"06:00 AM - 05:30 PM (Safari slots apply)\",\n    entryFee: \"₹100 per person + Safari charges\",\n    xpReward: 180,\n    stampIcon: \"🐅\",\n    unlockClue: \"Explore the ancient Chero forts buried deep inside tiger territory.\",\n    heroImage: \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Entrance_of_Betla_national_park.jpg/1280px-Entrance_of_Betla_national_park.jpg\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Entrance_of_Betla_national_park.jpg/1280px-Entrance_of_Betla_national_park.jpg\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Entrance_of_Betla_national_park.jpg/1280px-Entrance_of_Betla_national_park.jpg\"\n    ],\n    description: \"One of the earliest national parks in India to come under Project Tiger in 1974, Betla spans rolling hills, teak groves, and dense sal forests. Deep inside the jungle stand the mysterious twin 16th-century Palamu Forts built by the sovereign Chero kings, blending royal Mughal-tribal stone architecture with untamed wilderness.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"Elephant-back and 4x4 open safari tracks\",\n      \"Historic 16th-century Chero Dynasty jungle forts\",\n      \"Diverse wildlife: Elephants, leopards, gaur (Indian bison), chital & sloth bears\",\n      \"Lush tropical deciduous vegetation and natural waterholes\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Ranchi Birsa Munda Airport (165 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Daltonganj Railway Station (25 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Regular private and state buses run from Ranchi, Daltonganj, and Netarhat\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Always hire a registered forest department naturalist guide and stay strictly inside safari vehicles on track routes.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Do not venture into fort ruins on foot without forest rangers; wild elephants and sloth bears frequent the forest corridor after sunset.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"Betla's name is an acronym: B-Bison, E-Elephant, T-Tiger, L-Leopard, A-Axis axis (Chital).\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"dassam-falls\",\n    name: \"Dassam Falls\",\n    tagline: \"Ten torrential streams plummeting into Kanchi gorge\",\n    category: \"Waterfall & Adventure\",\n    district: \"Ranchi\",\n    location: \"Taimara village, 34 km from Ranchi\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.1436,\n      lng: 85.4667\n    },\n    elevation: \"310 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"October to March\",\n    timings: \"08:00 AM - 05:00 PM\",\n    entryFee: \"₹15 per person\",\n    xpReward: 140,\n    stampIcon: \"💦\",\n    unlockClue: \"Stand upon the glass cantilever bridge as Kanchi river splits in ten.\",\n    heroImage: \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Dassam_falls.jpg/1280px-Dassam_falls.jpg\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Dassam_falls.jpg/1280px-Dassam_falls.jpg\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Dassam_falls.jpg/1280px-Dassam_falls.jpg\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Originally known as 'Da-song' in the local Mundari tribal dialect ('Da' meaning water, 'Song' meaning pouring out), Dassam Falls drops 44 meters over sheer granite cliffs. The Kanchi River splits into ten distinct sparkling streams before roaring into a deep forested canyon.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"44-meter natural cascade splitting into ten distinct streams\",\n      \"Glass skywalk & newly built cantilevered viewing bridges\",\n      \"Dramatic acoustic echo through the canyon amphitheatre\",\n      \"Surrounding virgin Sal and Mahua woodland trails\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Ranchi Airport (35 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Ranchi Junction (34 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Smooth drive along Ranchi-Tata Highway (NH-33) turning right at Taimara\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Stay behind the designated stainless steel safety railing and glass viewpoints at all times.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Swimming or bathing in the plunge pool is strictly prohibited; the underwater current has hidden cavernous under-tows.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"The name Dassam is a corruption of the Mundari phrase 'Da-Song' referring to 10 cascading streams.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"jonha-falls\",\n    name: \"Jonha Falls (Gautamdhara)\",\n    tagline: \"Hanging valley cascade where Lord Buddha rested\",\n    category: \"Waterfall & Adventure\",\n    district: \"Ranchi\",\n    location: \"Jonha, 40 km East of Ranchi\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.3444,\n      lng: 85.6072\n    },\n    elevation: \"290 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"October to February\",\n    timings: \"06:00 AM - 05:00 PM\",\n    entryFee: \"₹10 per person\",\n    xpReward: 130,\n    stampIcon: \"🧘\",\n    unlockClue: \"Discover the sacred Buddhist sanctuary above the hanging valley knickpoint.\",\n    heroImage: \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/17/Jonha_falls.jpg\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/17/Jonha_falls.jpg\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/17/Jonha_falls.jpg\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Also called Gautamdhara, Jonha Falls is a classic hanging valley waterfall created where the Raru River drops 43 meters to join the main plateau basin. A tranquil Buddhist shrine sits above the 722 stone steps, commemorating the belief that Gautama Buddha bathed here during his journeys across Magadha.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"43-meter hanging valley waterfall surrounded by forested knolls\",\n      \"Historical Buddhist Ashram and shrine on the upper cliff\",\n      \"Spectacular rock pools and broad stepping stones\",\n      \"Picturesque weekly tribal haat (market) on Tuesdays and Saturdays\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Birsa Munda Airport Ranchi (42 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Jonha Railway Station (1.5 km) or Ranchi Junction (40 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"40 km drive via Ranchi-Purulia highway with scenic forest stretches\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Take breaks when climbing back up the 722 stone stairs; keep hydration handy.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Do not climb onto the slippery rock ledges directly beside the upper fall crest.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"Jonha is an example of an edge knickpoint waterfall created by geological rejuvenation of the Chotanagpur river system.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"netarhat\",\n    name: \"Netarhat (Queen of Chotanagpur)\",\n    tagline: \"The famous hill station crowned in mist, pine & legendary sunrises\",\n    category: \"Mountain Peaks\",\n    district: \"Latehar\",\n    location: \"Western Plateau, 154 km from Ranchi\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.4833,\n      lng: 84.2667\n    },\n    elevation: \"1,128 m (3,700 ft)\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"Year-Round (Best Oct - March for clear sunrises)\",\n    timings: \"Open 24 Hours\",\n    entryFee: \"Free\",\n    xpReward: 190,\n    stampIcon: \"🌲\",\n    unlockClue: \"Catch the legendary Magnolia Point sunset over Koel river valley.\",\n    heroImage: \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/ce/Pine_trees_of_Netarhat_Hill_station.jpg\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/ce/Pine_trees_of_Netarhat_Hill_station.jpg\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/ce/Pine_trees_of_Netarhat_Hill_station.jpg\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Perched atop an expansive flat laterite plateau at 1,128 meters, Netarhat is the undisputed 'Queen of Chotanagpur'. Celebrated for its crisp alpine weather, fragrant British pine plantations, and the iconic Magnolia Sunset Point, it is Jharkhand's premier hill destination.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"Magnolia Point: Famous sunset overlooking the vast Koel River valley\",\n      \"Pine forest walks with morning mist and fresh mountain resin\",\n      \"Upper & Lower Ghaghri waterfalls nestled in Sal forests\",\n      \"Cool hill climate with winter temperatures touching near freezing\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Ranchi Birsa Munda Airport (154 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Lohardaga Railway Station (85 km) or Ranchi (154 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Mesmerizing hill drive from Ranchi through Lohardaga with scenic forested ghats\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Carry warm woollens between November and February as temperatures drop sharply after sunset.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Avoid driving through isolated forest ghat sections late at night; plan your mountain transit during daylight hours.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"The British named it 'Nature's Hat' due to its bowl-shaped plateau topography, which evolved into Netarhat.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"lodh-falls\",\n    name: \"Lodh Falls (Burha Ghaag)\",\n    tagline: \"The highest waterfall in Jharkhand (143 meters)\",\n    category: \"Waterfall & Adventure\",\n    district: \"Latehar\",\n    location: \"Near Mahuadanr, 195 km from Ranchi\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.5500,\n      lng: 84.0500\n    },\n    elevation: \"450 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"September to February\",\n    timings: \"08:00 AM - 04:30 PM\",\n    entryFee: \"₹10 per person\",\n    xpReward: 220,\n    stampIcon: \"⚡\",\n    unlockClue: \"Hear the acoustic thunder of Jharkhand's tallest 143-meter giant.\",\n    heroImage: \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Lodh_Fall.png/1280px-Lodh_Fall.png\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Lodh_Fall.png/1280px-Lodh_Fall.png\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Lodh_Fall.png/1280px-Lodh_Fall.png\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Tumbling from a staggering height of 143 meters (469 feet) across multiple stepped tiers on the Burha River, Lodh Falls is the 21st highest waterfall in India and the highest in Jharkhand. Enveloped by pristine forests, its acoustic rumble echoes for miles.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"Highest waterfall in Jharkhand with a 143-meter multi-tiered plunge\",\n      \"Natural amphitheater surrounded by primeval Sal forests\",\n      \"Pristine ecotourism sanctuary with rich birdlife and orchids\",\n      \"Iconic thunderous roar heard from kilometers away\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Ranchi Airport (195 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Daltonganj Railway Station (120 km) or Latehar (90 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Accessible via Mahuadanr valley road from Netarhat (60 km) or Daltonganj\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Fuel up your vehicle completely before leaving Mahuadanr or Netarhat; no fuel stations on interior forest tracks.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Do not attempt to cross river rapids or climb upper tiers; water surge is powerful and swift.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"The acoustic rumble of Lodh Falls is so powerful in peak flow that locals call it 'The Thunder of Chotanagpur'.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"dalma-wildlife-sanctuary\",\n    name: \"Dalma Wildlife Sanctuary\",\n    tagline: \"Hilltop elephant sanctuary overlooking Jamshedpur\",\n    category: \"Wildlife & Nature\",\n    district: \"East Singhbhum\",\n    location: \"Dalma Hills, 10 km from Jamshedpur\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 22.9000,\n      lng: 86.2167\n    },\n    elevation: \"926 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"October to April\",\n    timings: \"07:00 AM - 05:00 PM\",\n    entryFee: \"₹50 per person + Vehicle pass\",\n    xpReward: 160,\n    stampIcon: \"🐘\",\n    unlockClue: \"Ascend 926 meters to the elephant lookout above steel city.\",\n    heroImage: \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Wild_Abode.jpg/1280px-Wild_Abode.jpg\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Wild_Abode.jpg/1280px-Wild_Abode.jpg\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Wild_Abode.jpg/1280px-Wild_Abode.jpg\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Spread over 195 sq km across the Dalma mountain range towering 926 meters high, this sanctuary is famous for its resident Asian elephant population, barking deer, leopards, and ancient hilltop Shiva temple. The viewpoint at the summit provides breathtaking vistas of Jamshedpur glowing beside the Subarnarekha River.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"Dalma Summit Viewpoint with panoramic 360-degree plains views\",\n      \"Natural elephant habitat and canopy bird observation towers\",\n      \"Hilltop Shiva temple visited by forest pilgrims for generations\",\n      \"Pindrabera Forest Rest House perched above the valley\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Ranchi Birsa Munda Airport (125 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Tatanagar Junction Jamshedpur (18 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Smoothly accessible from NH-33 just 10 km north of Jamshedpur city\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Carry binoculars and drive under 20 km/h inside sanctuary limits to avoid startling wildlife.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Entry is closed after 5:00 PM; strictly adhere to ranger instructions regarding elephant herd movements.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"During the annual Sendra festival, tribal trackers traverse these hills in a tradition that predates modern recorded history.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"tagore-hill\",\n    name: \"Tagore Hill (Morabadi)\",\n    tagline: \"The philosopher's hill of the Tagore family in Ranchi\",\n    category: \"Spiritual & Heritage\",\n    district: \"Ranchi\",\n    location: \"Morabadi, Ranchi City\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.4022,\n      lng: 85.3356\n    },\n    elevation: \"650 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"October to March (Mesmerizing at Sunrise/Sunset)\",\n    timings: \"06:00 AM - 06:30 PM\",\n    entryFee: \"₹10 per person\",\n    xpReward: 110,\n    stampIcon: \"📜\",\n    unlockClue: \"Walk the rocky knoll where Jyotirindranath Tagore translated timeless classics.\",\n    heroImage: \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Tagore_hill_Ranchi.jpg/1280px-Tagore_hill_Ranchi.jpg\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Tagore_hill_Ranchi.jpg/1280px-Tagore_hill_Ranchi.jpg\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Tagore_hill_Ranchi.jpg/1280px-Tagore_hill_Ranchi.jpg\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Rising 300 feet above the Ranchi plateau in Morabadi, Tagore Hill was the cherished sanctuary of Jyotirindranath Tagore (elder brother of Rabindranath Tagore). Here, atop the granite knoll, he built 'Shanti Dham' in 1908 and translated celebrated philosophical classics in total contemplation.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"Shanti Dham: Historic stone pavilion perched at the rocky peak\",\n      \"Brahmo Mandir and Tagore Art & Cultural exhibition museum\",\n      \"Sweeping panoramic vistas over Ranchi city and Morabadi grounds\",\n      \"Peaceful shaded stone pathways perfect for contemplative walks\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Birsa Munda Airport Ranchi (12 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Ranchi Railway Station (7 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Centrally situated in Morabadi, easily accessible by auto-rickshaw or taxi\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Take care when stepping on open granite surfaces during wet monsoon showers.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Do not climb beyond designated boundary walls or railings on the cliff overlook.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"Rabindranath Tagore visited his brother here and drew deep inspiration from the Chotanagpur forest landscape for parts of 'Gitanjali'.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"maithon-dam\",\n    name: \"Maithon Dam & Lake\",\n    tagline: \"The serene 'Mother's Abode' with blue water islands and speedboating\",\n    category: \"Scenic & Lakes\",\n    district: \"Dhanbad\",\n    location: \"Barakar River, 48 km from Dhanbad\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.7844,\n      lng: 86.8153\n    },\n    elevation: \"156 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"October to March\",\n    timings: \"06:00 AM - 06:00 PM\",\n    entryFee: \"Free (Boating charges apply)\",\n    xpReward: 130,\n    stampIcon: \"⛵\",\n    unlockClue: \"Speedboat across the blue lake to the secluded Green Island (Sabuj Dweep).\",\n    heroImage: \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Maithon_dam%2C_india.jpg/1280px-Maithon_dam%2C_india.jpg\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Maithon_dam%2C_india.jpg/1280px-Maithon_dam%2C_india.jpg\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Maithon_dam%2C_india.jpg/1280px-Maithon_dam%2C_india.jpg\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Built over the Barakar River, Maithon ('Mai-ka-than' or Mother's Abode) features a massive 65-square-kilometer blue reservoir dotted with green islands, an underground power station, and the ancient Kalyaneshwari Temple.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"65 sq km blue water lake with speedboating to Sabuj Dweep (Green Island)\",\n      \"India's first unique underground hydel power station\",\n      \"Centuries-old sacred Kalyaneshwari Temple located nearby\",\n      \"Picturesque sunrise and sunset views over tranquil reservoir waters\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Kazi Nazrul Islam Airport Durgapur (60 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Kumardhubi Station (5 km) or Dhanbad Junction (45 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Conveniently located 8 km off the Grand Trunk Road (NH-19)\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Always wear life jackets provided during boat rides across the deep reservoir channels.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Strictly avoid venturing close to spillway gates and intake towers where strong suction currents operate.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"Maithon Dam was inaugurated by Prime Minister Jawaharlal Nehru in 1957 as part of the historic Damodar Valley Project.\"\n  }\n];\n\n// Curated Informational Micro-Moments (\"Did You Know?\" editorial facts)\nconst DID_YOU_KNOW_FACTS = [\n  {\n    number: \"01\",\n    tag: \"ETYMOLOGY & NATURE\",\n    headline: \"Jharkhand literally means 'The Territory of Forests'\",\n    body: \"Derived from 'Jhar' (dense forest/bushland) and 'Khand' (land), over 29% of the state's geographical area is enveloped in primeval Sal, Mahua, and Teak woodland canopy.\"\n  },\n  {\n    number: \"02\",\n    tag: \"INDIGENOUS HERITAGE\",\n    headline: \"Home to 32 Unique Indigenous Tribal Communities\",\n    body: \"Rich in living ancestral wisdom, Jharkhand's Santhal, Munda, Oraon, Ho, and Birhor tribes maintain continuous thousand-year traditions in harmony with Mother Nature (Marang Buru).\"\n  },\n  {\n    number: \"03\",\n    tag: \"LIVING ART FORMS\",\n    headline: \"GI-Tagged Sohrai & Khovar Murals Painted with Natural Earth\",\n    body: \"Tribal women paint intricate ritual wall art using naturally sourced manganese black, ochre yellow, and white kaolin clay, a tradition dating back to prehistoric rock art.\"\n  },\n  {\n    number: \"04\",\n    tag: \"GEOLOGICAL WONDERS\",\n    headline: \"The Chotanagpur Plateau is over 2.5 Billion Years Old\",\n    body: \"Part of the ancient Gondwanaland supercontinent, this dramatic plateau features stepped knickpoints creating dozens of pristine waterfalls cascading across ancient granite.\"\n  }\n];\n\n// Travel Themes for Experience Showcase\nconst TRAVEL_THEMES = [\n  {\n    id: \"waterfalls\",\n    title: \"Roaring Waterfalls & Canyons\",\n    subtitle: \"From 143-meter thunderous plunges to serene emerald pools\",\n    count: \"15+ Cascades\",\n    image: \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Hundru_Falls%2C_Jharkhand%2C_India_4.jpg/1280px-Hundru_Falls%2C_Jharkhand%2C_India_4.jpg\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"wilderness\",\n    title: \"Untamed Wildlife & Sal Forests\",\n    subtitle: \"Asia's densest Sal reserves, wild elephant herds and tigers\",\n    count: \"4 Sanctuaries\",\n    image: \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Entrance_of_Betla_national_park.jpg/1280px-Entrance_of_Betla_national_park.jpg\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"spiritual\",\n    title: \"Sacred Summits & Ancient Shrines\",\n    subtitle: \"Revered Jyotirlingas, Jain mountain peaks, and timeless pilgrimages\",\n    count: \"8 Holy Sites\",\n    image: \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Baidyanath_temple_and_temple_complex%2C_Deoghar_04.jpg/1280px-Baidyanath_temple_and_temple_complex%2C_Deoghar_04.jpg\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"scenic\",\n    title: \"Serpentine Ghats & Misty Pine Peaks\",\n    subtitle: \"Patratu hairpin roads, Netarhat sunrises and hilltop horizons\",\n    count: \"10 Viewpoints\",\n    image: \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Patratu_Valley_at_night.jpg/1280px-Patratu_Valley_at_night.jpg\"\n  }\n];\n","Description":"Update data.js with actual Wikimedia photos and passport unlock metadata","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\Bhavish Sawant\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\jharkhand-tourism\\js\\data.js","toolAction":"Updating data.js","toolSummary":"Updating data.js"}}]}
